* * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
* PDA:      PDAVALID
* SYSTEM:   SIFAP - PAYMENT INSPECTION AND ADMINISTRATION SYSTEM
* AUTHOR:   MARCIA HELENA OLIVEIRA
* DATE:     12/03/1998
* CHANGED:  22/09/2003 - ANA LUCIA      - ADD SPECIAL DOC INDICATOR
* CHANGED:  07/06/2011 - ROBERTO MENDES - ADD NIS FIELD
* PURPOSE:  PARAMETER AREA FOR THE BENEFICIARY DOCUMENT
*           VALIDATION SUBPROGRAM FAMILY.
*           USED BY SUBVALCP (CPF) AND SUBVALNI (NIS/PIS).
*
* USE IN CALLER:
*           DEFINE DATA
*             LOCAL USING PDAVALID
*             LOCAL
*               1 ... PROGRAM-SPECIFIC FIELDS ...
*           END-DEFINE
*
* USE IN CALLEE:
*           DEFINE DATA
*             PARAMETER USING PDAVALID
*             LOCAL
*               1 ... WORK FIELDS ...
*           END-DEFINE
*
* STANDARD: NT-SUPDE-011/1998 - ONE PDA PER ROUTINE FAMILY.
*           BOTH SUBPROGRAMS RECEIVE THE SAME LIST IN THE
*           SAME ORDER. A FIELD UNUSED BY THE CALLEE IS
*           IGNORED - THIS IS INTENTIONAL, NOT A DEFECT.
*
* RETURN CODES (#PV-COD-RETURN):
*           0000 - VALID DOCUMENT
*           1001 - INVALID CPF - CHECK DIGIT
*           1002 - CPF NOT PROVIDED
*           1003 - CPF WITH ALL DIGITS EQUAL
*           1004 - INVALID DOCUMENT TYPE FOR THIS ROUTINE
*           1005 - CPF CONTAINS NONNUMERIC CHARACTER
*           1010 - NIS NOT PROVIDED
*           1011 - INVALID NIS - CHECK DIGIT
*           1012 - NIS CONTAINS NONNUMERIC CHARACTER
*           9999 - NATURAL ERROR - SEE CMPRINT
* * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * * *
DEFINE DATA PARAMETER
*
* --- INPUT ---
*
1 #PV-TYPE-DOC            (A1)    /* IN  C=CPF  N=NIS/PIS/PASEP
1 #PV-CPF                 (A11)   /* IN  UNMASKED CPF, LEFT-PADDED
1 #PV-NIS                 (A11)   /* IN  UNMASKED NIS/PIS/PASEP
*
* --- OUTPUT ---
*
1 #PV-COD-RETURN          (N4)    /* OUT 0000 = VALID
1 #PV-MSG                 (A60)   /* OUT BLANK WHEN VALID
1 #PV-IND-SPECIAL         (A1)    /* OUT S=SPECIAL DOC N=COMMON DOC
*
END-DEFINE
